{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "expand-day-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7d, the timespan dimension: the `expand-day` run computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE through `moves-onroad.esm`. It is the second RunSpec this domain document has been asked for and the first that is not `process-tirewear`, so it is where the 7c split stops being a rearrangement of one fixture and starts being a model.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES, which §23 asks for before a dimension is called covered.\n\n* THE DAY AXIS AT BOTH OF ITS VALUES. `runspecday` is 2 rows here and 1 everywhere else in this tree, so a model that hardcoded a day-keyed quantity passed the whole suite until now. Nothing in `onroad/model.esm` changed to accept it: `n_runspecday` is discovered from the source's own extent, and the activity relation, the hour-day key and the output relation all double by themselves.\n\n* A SELECTED POLLUTANT-PROCESS THAT EMITS NOTHING. The RunSpec asks for 9101, 9102 and 9190; `MOVESOutput` carries 250 rows of 91-01 and not one row of the other two, because start exhaust and extended idle write their rates on the off-network road type 1 and this run selects road type 4 alone (docs/mixed-onroad.md §0.2). `process-tirewear` could not discriminate that -- all three of its pollutant-processes happen on a road -- and the model now reads the rule out of `emissionprocess.occursOnRealRoads` instead of assuming a rectangular output.\n\nTHE TEN SELECTIONS, ONE BINDING AND THE ORACLE are everything this document carries. Against `runspecs/process-tirewear.esm` it differs in ten `url_template`s and the value of `n_outputPolProcess`, which is the measurement PLAN.md §7.1 wanted: a per-fixture document holds selections and nothing mechanical. `fixtures/expand-day.esm` is the same run written the other way -- 14,603 lines, 46 data sources and 196 equations, of which 147 are byte-identical to `fixtures/process-tirewear.esm`'s -- and it stays in the tree as a snapshot-fed module test (PLAN.md §7.6), not as the way a second run gets added.\n\nWHY `n_outputPolProcess` IS A BINDING and not a discovered extent: it is the count of pollutant-processes whose rates survive the road-type join, which no table in the database states -- MOVES computes it. `outputPolProcessCount` recomputes it from the chain, exactly as `cohortSurvivorCount` recomputes `n_outputCohort`, so the declaration is checked rather than trusted.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "expand-day"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_runspecyear": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/expand-day/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecyear.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecyear"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, yearID 2020. The scope comes from these tables and never from the RunSpec XML, whose @key attributes are 0-based indices into sorted ID lists (docs/mixed-onroad.md §0.1).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecmonth": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/expand-day/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecmonth.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecmonth"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, monthID 8.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspechour": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/expand-day/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspechour.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspechour"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, hourID 7 -- 6am-7am, colder than `mixed-onroad`'s 9. The heat index is 59.5 degF against 66.9, which crosses the EV temperature quadratic's nearer zero at 63.964 degF and reaches the regClassID-0 wildcard row of `temperatureadjustment` on every electricity row (docs/expand-day.md).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_aggregationhour": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/expand-day/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspechour.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_aggregationhour"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "The hours the run aggregates over. This run does not set `aggregateBy`, so it is `runspechour` itself and the same file.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecday": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/expand-day/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecday.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecday"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "2 ROWS, dayID 2 (weekend) and 5 (weekday), AND THAT IS WHY THIS RUN IS HERE. Every other RunSpec in this tree selects one day type, so a model that hardcoded `noOfRealDays` 5, `hourDayID` 75 or four rows of `dayVMTFraction` passed the whole suite; 28 of the 42 snapshots selected both by ACCIDENT before the RunSpec correction and now select one on purpose (moves.rs PR #55, docs/esm-conventions.md §42.5). `n_runspecday` is discovered from this extent, so the activity relation and the output relation double with no edit to the model.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_rateday": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/expand-day/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecday.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_rateday"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "The day types the RATE-side time pre-aggregation is scoped to. This run does not set `aggregateBy`, so it is `runspecday` itself and the same file: the pre-aggregation averages over one cell and returns the table's own value. A run that aggregates points this somewhere else, because MOVES overwrites `runspecday` with the synthesized output day AFTER the pre-aggregation has run.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_actday": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/expand-day/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecday.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_actday"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "The day types the output day's ACTIVITY covers. This run does not set `aggregateBy`, so it is `runspecday` itself and the same file, and `noOfRealDays` is that one day type's.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecsourcetype": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/expand-day/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecsourcetype.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecsourcetype"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, sourceTypeID 21.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecroadtype": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/expand-day/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecroadtype.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecroadtype"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, roadTypeID 4, AND IT IS THE SECOND REASON THIS RUN IS HERE. `BaseRateCalculator` joins its rate rows to `runSpecRoadType`; start exhaust and extended idle write theirs on the off-network road type 1; so 9102 and 9190 are discarded entire and `MOVESOutput` carries the running-exhaust block alone (docs/mixed-onroad.md §0.2). `emissionprocess.occursOnRealRoads` is the other half of that join and the model reads it rather than listing process ids.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecsourcefueltype": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/expand-day/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecsourcefueltype.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecsourcefueltype"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope",
          "cohorts"
        ],
        "note": "4 rows: gasoline, diesel, E85 and electricity. The second factor of the cohort candidate grid.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecpollutantprocess": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/expand-day/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecpollutantprocess.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecpollutantprocess"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "3 rows: 9101, 9102 and 9190 -- Total Energy Consumption on running exhaust, start exhaust and extended idle. ONE of them emits. This is the first run in the tree whose selected pollutant-process set is larger than its output's, which is what makes `rspp_isEmitted` a check rather than a constant 1.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecchainedto": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/expand-day/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecchainedto.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecchainedto"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope",
          "chain"
        ],
        "note": "0 rows: nothing in this run is chained. `process-tirewear` has one (10710 <- 11710) and this has none, so the left join onto it returns the additive identity for every pollutant-process and the chain term vanishes without a branch.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspeccounty": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/expand-day/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspeccounty.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspeccounty"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, countyID 26161. What narrows the national `Link`'s 22,610 rows to this run's one, together with the road type (PLAN.md §7.3.3).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_movesoutput": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/expand-day/tables/db__out_expand_day__movesoutput.parquet"
      },
      "reader_options": {
        "float_columns": [
          "emissionQuant"
        ]
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "oracle",
          "expected-output"
        ],
        "note": "The 250-row expected output: running-exhaust Total Energy Consumption for 125 (modelYearID, fuelTypeID) cohorts on each of two day types. DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING -- reading it would transcribe the answer and its extent would transcribe the answer's shape. compare-output.py reads it directly under tolerance.toml.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    }
  },
